<title>GERMANY: Economy not growing enough to create jobs - Jagoda.</title>
<headline>Economy not growing enough to create jobs - Jagoda.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's economic growth in May was insufficient to revive its flagging jobs market, Labour Office President Bernhard Jagoda said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The seasonal revival in the German jobs market stopped in May. As before, the driving forces of the economy are insufficient to bring about a turnaround in the jobs market,&quot; he said after the office released figures showing seasonally adjusted unemployment rose by 56,000 in May to 4.358 million.</p>
<p>- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
